{"schema":"clawhub.skill.verify.v1","ok":false,"decision":"fail","reasons":["security.status_not_clean"],"slug":"contact-discovery","displayName":"Lead Contact Finder","pageUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/jernejcicorbin-hub/skills/contact-discovery","publisherHandle":"jernejcicorbin-hub","publisherDisplayName":"jernejcicorbin-hub","publisherProfileUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/jernejcicorbin-hub","version":"1.0.0","resolvedFrom":"version","tag":null,"createdAt":1778619902823,"card":{"available":true,"path":"skill-card.md","url":"https://wry-manatee-359.convex.site/api/v1/skills/contact-discovery/card?ownerHandle=jernejcicorbin-hub&version=1.0.0","sha256":"426b3036139a62ba250c26d29bbca89cbb9c50c50a3c32a3252dc619f96602cd","size":2331,"contentType":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8"},"artifact":{"sourceFingerprint":"252d524658ce8b3d7fe4acdabef1092a1aa67579786d35166b88fb0bdf058120","bundleFingerprints":["ec9523b64bc3f098b9da3b4562558fdb122477018a1e384a605c71947c215d0e","c3cc7dd106fcc47160987b662b68589943f41c0cf6bba3f843d62f05cdf10d27"],"files":[{"path":"_meta.json","size":427,"sha256":"05c1522b18e558147ded22664985ef1c1c761698e713b8460f8c882c5cf350f3","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"README.md","size":3398,"sha256":"dbc8d1f2163b8aad866f5522e750f15c97a82a9fbf9edd6de57b1c951bfc08bc","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":7249,"sha256":"bc856c4190f5f428f51c10df5828bcfe197d2b2de3547b494f1efcc5a16dca6c","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"contact-find.sh","size":19174,"sha256":"5c5c45eb27a97e1080174909c11367253a59f3583a0b3f74552e8eeafcd0dae6","contentType":"text/x-sh"},{"path":"hooks/contact-discovery/handler.js","size":1446,"sha256":"0c73de555536bed863c00bfae719f71275a3a0f06be6b885c4eb955ba9085691","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"hooks/contact-discovery/HOOK.md","size":340,"sha256":"9fd5e40a1f9727386259483cb74faf0c09ea997680af25c7adebdf3f7d508194","contentType":"text/markdown"}]},"provenance":{"source":"unavailable","reason":"No server-resolved GitHub import provenance is stored for this version."},"security":{"status":"suspicious","passed":false,"rawStatus":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill mostly does what it says, but needs review because it handles a Prismfy API key in ways that can expose the key if users follow the setup or override endpoints unsafely.","model":null,"checkedAt":1789545881289,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.1","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[{"ruleId":"T09","level":"error","message":{"text":"Bearer API Credential Can Be Transmitted to an Untrusted Configurable Endpoint"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"contact-find.sh"},"region":{"startLine":4,"endLine":203}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"95214060c0c4a9c0"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n**File Location**: `contact-find.sh`, lines 4–9, 76–87, and 199–203  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Unvalidated credential-bearing request destination  \n**Risk Level**: High\n\n### Vulnerable Code\n\n```bash\nAPI_URL=\"${PRISMFY_API_URL:-https://api.prismfy.io/v1/search}\"\nAPI_URL=\"${API_URL%/}\"\nAPI_ROOT=\"${PRISMFY_API_ROOT:-}\"\nAPI_ROOT=\"${API_ROOT%/}\"\nME_URL=\"${PRISMFY_ME_URL:-}\"\nME_URL=\"${ME_URL%/}\"\n```\n\n```bash\nif [[ \"$quota\" -eq 1 ]]; then\n  [[ -n \"${PRISMFY_API_KEY:-}\" ]] || die \"PRISMFY_API_KEY is not set\"\n  if [[ -z \"$ME_URL\" ]]; then\n    if [[ -n \"$API_ROOT\" ]]; then\n      ME_URL=\"${API_ROOT}/user/me\"\n    elif [[ \"$API_URL\" == */search ]]; then\n      ME_URL=\"${API_URL%/search}/user/me\"\n    else\n      die \"cannot derive quota endpoint from PRISMFY_API_URL; set PRISMFY_API_ROOT or PRISMFY_ME_URL\"\n    fi\n  fi\n  curl -fsS -H \"Authorization: Bearer $PRISMFY_API_KEY\" \"$ME_URL\"\n  exit 0\nfi\n```\n\n```bash\nif response=\"$(curl -m 20 -fsS \"$API_URL\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $PRISMFY_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d \"$payload\" 2>\"$err\")\"; then\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe script takes request destinations from the `PRISMFY_API_URL`, `PRISMFY_API_ROOT`, and `PRISMFY_ME_URL` environment variables. It does not validate their URL schemes, hostnames, ports, or trust relationships before attaching the `PRISMFY_API_KEY` as a bearer credential.\n\nConsequently, any party able to influence the process environment or the wrapper used to invoke this script can redirect authenticated requests to an arbitrary destination. The risk is especially significant because the authorization header is added unconditionally after only checking that the API key is present. The search request also includes person, company, domain, role, and geographic query data in its JSON payload.\n\nThe default endpoint is the expected Prismfy HTTPS service, so exploitation requires influence over configuration or the invocation environment. This is nevertheless a dangerous trust-boundary failure because configurable destinations and credentials are combined without validation.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. An attacker gains the ability to influence the environment used to launch the skill, such as through an unsafe wrapper, deployment configuration, compromised shell profile, or agent runtime configuration.\n2. The attacker sets `PRISMFY_API_URL` or `PRISMFY_ME_URL` to an attacker-controlled server. Alternatively, the attacker sets `PRISMFY_API_ROOT`, which is used to derive the quota endpoint.\n3. A user or agent invokes `contact-find.sh` for a search or quota check.\n4. The script sends `Authorization: Bearer $PRISMFY_API_KEY` to the attacker-controlled destination.\n5. For search operations, the attacker also receives the JSON query payload containing the contact-discovery inputs.\n6. The attacker can reuse the disclosed key against the legitimate service until it is revoked or expires.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nSuccessful exploitation can disclose the Prismfy API key and permit unauthorized API use within the privileges and quota assigned to that key. This can cause quota consumption, unauthorized searches, service charges where applicable, and loss of confidentiality for submitted person or company queries.\n\nThe flaw does not directly grant operating-system privileges or arbitrary local code execution. Its scope is limited to the exposed API credential, associated Prismfy permissions, and data transmitted through redirected requests.\n]]>","severity":"High"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Require HTTPS for every credential-bearing endpoint.\n2. Parse and validate each URL before issuing a request.\n3. Allowlist trusted Prismfy hostnames and reject user information, unexpected ports, redirects to untrusted hosts, malformed URLs, and non-HTTPS schemes.\n4. Disable or tightly constrain redirects. If redirects are required, validate the destination before forwarding the authorization header.\n5. Do not attach the Prismfy credential to arbitrary custom endpoints.\n6. If private or enterprise endpoints must be supported, require explicit opt-in configuration and use a separate credential scoped to that endpoint.\n7. Document all endpoint override variables and their security implications.\n8. Consider pinning the normal API endpoint in code and exposing overrides only through a trusted administrator-controlled configuration source.\n9. Rotate the API key if there is any indication that the script was run with an untrusted endpoint.\n\nAn appropriate validation policy should ensure that the final URL is HTTPS and that its normalized hostname belongs to an explicit trusted set before constructing the authorization header.\n]]>"}}]},{"ruleId":"T09","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Documentation Recommends Persistent Plaintext Storage of the API Key"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"SKILL.md"},"region":{"startLine":48,"endLine":51}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"313d816d38652ce9"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n**File Location**: `SKILL.md`, lines 48–51; `README.md`, lines 62–67  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Insecure secret-storage guidance  \n**Risk Level**: Medium\n\n### Vulnerable Code\n\n`SKILL.md`:\n\n```bash\necho 'export PRISMFY_API_KEY=\"ss_live_your_key_here\"' >> ~/.bashrc\nsource ~/.bashrc\n```\n\n`README.md`:\n\n```bash\necho 'export PRISMFY_API_KEY=\"ss_live_your_key_here\"' >> ~/.bashrc\nsource ~/.bashrc\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe setup instructions recommend writing a long-lived API credential directly into `~/.bashrc`. This stores the key as plaintext in a commonly read and frequently backed-up shell configuration file.\n\nShell startup files may be collected in support bundles, copied between systems, synchronized as dotfiles, committed accidentally to source control, or exposed to other local accounts if permissions are too broad. Sourcing the file also exports the secret to subsequently launched child processes, increasing the number of processes that can access it.\n\nThe issue is not a hardcoded credential in the package—the displayed value is an example—but the prescribed storage method encourages users to persist their real credential in an insufficiently protected location.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. A user follows the documented persistent-setup instructions and substitutes a valid Prismfy API key.\n2. The key is stored in plaintext in `~/.bashrc`.\n3. A local process or user with read access, a backup consumer, a support-bundle recipient, a dotfile synchronization service, or an accidental repository publication obtains the file.\n4. The observer extracts the API key from the exported environment assignment.\n5. The disclosed key can be reused against Prismfy until it expires or is revoked.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nExposure grants the attacker the API permissions and quota associated with the compromised Prismfy key. Potential consequences include unauthorized searches, quota depletion, charges where applicable, and activity being attributed to the victim.\n\nThis finding does not independently provide elevated operating-system privileges. Exploitation depends on access to the startup file, its copies, or environments derived from it, and its scope is limited to the permissions of the stored credential.\n]]>","severity":"Medium"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Replace the shell-profile recommendation with an operating-system credential manager, an OpenClaw secret store, or another dedicated secrets-management facility.\n2. Inject the key only into the process that requires it rather than exporting it globally to all descendant processes.\n3. If an environment file must be supported:\n   - store it outside the project and synchronized dotfile directories;\n   - restrict permissions to the owning user, such as mode `0600`;\n   - exclude it from source control, backups, diagnostics, and support bundles where possible;\n   - load it only for this skill rather than from a general interactive shell profile.\n4. Warn users never to commit or share files containing the key.\n5. Document credential rotation and revocation procedures.\n6. Recommend a narrowly scoped key with minimal quota and permissions.\n7. Update both `SKILL.md` and `README.md` so their setup guidance remains consistent.\n]]>"}}]}],"properties":{"securityScore":35,"primaryLanguage":"Markdown","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789545750.4335458,"endTime":1789545829.8890374}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"contact-discovery","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v57821ndx2y20mhw94vfg6rjs18egmes-tNns6w/clawscan-skillspector-3010885028/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-16T08:02:29.005369+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":66,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","max_issue_severity":"HIGH"},"components":[{"path":"README.md","type":"markdown","lines":135,"executable":false,"size_bytes":3398,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":247,"executable":false,"size_bytes":7249,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"_meta.json","type":"json","lines":19,"executable":false,"size_bytes":427,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"contact-find.sh","type":"shell","lines":529,"executable":true,"size_bytes":19174,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"hooks/contact-discovery/HOOK.md","type":"markdown","lines":9,"executable":false,"size_bytes":340,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"hooks/contact-discovery/handler.js","type":"javascript","lines":38,"executable":true,"size_bytes":1446,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"YR1","finding_id":"finding-d989e059f8c04a199d0526383387352f","category":"YARA Match","pattern":"YARA rule 'backdoor_persistence': Backdoor persistence with malicious payloads (shell commands, SSH key injection, hidden root users) [malware]","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.75,"location":{"file":"README.md","start_line":70,"end_line":null},"finding":"echo 'export PRISMFY_API_KEY=\"ss_live_your_key_here\"' >> ~/.bashrc","explanation":"YARA rule matched a known malware signature (reverse shell, backdoor, ransomware, C2 framework, or info stealer).","remediation":"Remove the malware payload or compromised file entirely. Investigate how it entered the skill and audit all other artifacts for additional indicators of compromise.","code_snippet":"ecking whether a person has a public email trail,\n- finding company email-format clues for later human review.\n\nNeed a key?\n- Get free search access and your API key at: https://prismfy.io\n\n## Setup\n\n1. Install the skill:\n```bash\nopenclaw skills install contact-discovery\n```\n\n2. Add your Prismfy API key:\n```bash\nexport PRISMFY_API_KEY=\"ss_live_your_key_here\"\n```\n\nTo keep it after restart:\n```bash\necho 'export PRISMFY_API_KEY=\"ss_live_your_key_here\"' >> ~/.bashrc\nsource ~/.bashrc\n```\n\nPreflight:\n- `PRISMFY_API_KEY` is set\n- `curl` and `jq` are installed\n\nAdvanced setup:\n- if quota lives on a different endpoint than search, set `PRISMFY_API_ROOT` or `PRISMFY_ME_URL`\n\n3. Verify API access:\n```bash\ncd ~/.openclaw/workspace/skills/contact-discovery\nbash contact-find.sh --quota\n```\n\n4. Quick smoke test:\n```bash\ncd ~/.openclaw/workspace/skills/contact-discovery\nbash contact-find.sh --company \"Vercel\" --query-family company\n```\n\n5. Export a JSON report:\n```bash\ncd ~/.openclaw/workspace/skills/","intent":null,"tags":["YARA Match","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"48e5e15990258e39da7c84daa4d117c50bb69726a92c750282221d519c2cd919","occurrences":[{"file":"README.md","start_line":70,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"YR1","finding_id":"finding-d989e059f8c04a199d0526383387352f","category":"YARA Match","pattern":"YARA rule 'backdoor_persistence': Backdoor persistence with malicious payloads (shell commands, SSH key injection, hidden root users) [malware]","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.75,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":53,"end_line":null},"finding":"echo 'export PRISMFY_API_KEY=\"ss_live_your_key_here\"' >> ~/.bashrc","explanation":"YARA rule matched a known malware signature (reverse shell, backdoor, ransomware, C2 framework, or info stealer).","remediation":"Remove the malware payload or compromised file entirely. Investigate how it entered the skill and audit all other artifacts for additional indicators of compromise.","code_snippet":"ecking whether a person has a public email trail,\n- finding company email-format clues for later human review.\n\nNeed a key?\n- Get free search access and your API key at: https://prismfy.io\n\n## Setup\n\n1. Install the skill:\n```bash\nopenclaw skills install contact-discovery\n```\n\n2. Add your Prismfy API key:\n```bash\nexport PRISMFY_API_KEY=\"ss_live_your_key_here\"\n```\n\nTo keep it after restart:\n```bash\necho 'export PRISMFY_API_KEY=\"ss_live_your_key_here\"' >> ~/.bashrc\nsource ~/.bashrc\n```\n\nPreflight:\n- `PRISMFY_API_KEY` is set\n- `curl` and `jq` are installed\n\nAdvanced setup:\n- if quota lives on a different endpoint than search, set `PRISMFY_API_ROOT` or `PRISMFY_ME_URL`\n\n3. Verify API access:\n```bash\ncd ~/.openclaw/workspace/skills/contact-discovery\nbash contact-find.sh --quota\n```\n\n4. Quick smoke test:\n```bash\ncd ~/.openclaw/workspace/skills/contact-discovery\nbash contact-find.sh --company \"Vercel\" --query-family company\n```\n\n5. Export a JSON report:\n```bash\ncd ~/.openclaw/workspace/skills/","intent":null,"tags":["YARA Match","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"48e5e15990258e39da7c84daa4d117c50bb69726a92c750282221d519c2cd919","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":53,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"LP3","finding_id":"finding-66a24f4d78b1454db9eef5c0103d06fc","category":"MCP Least Privilege","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"Without declared permissions the skill's intent is opaque and cannot be validated.","remediation":"Declare the skill's tool scope: for Claude Code / Agent Skills SKILL.md, list the tools the skill may invoke in the 'allowed-tools' frontmatter field; for MCP server manifests, add a 'permissions' list naming the required capabilities.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI02","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-0ac40006f8cd47f8b281c9328487679b","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"contact-find.sh","start_line":4,"end_line":null},"finding":"https://api.prismfy.io/","explanation":"Data is being sent to an external URL. This could be legitimate telemetry or data exfiltration. Manual review is recommended.","remediation":"Verify the destination URL is trusted and necessary. Remove or replace with documented APIs. Ensure no secrets, tokens, or PII are transmitted.","code_snippet":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\nset -euo pipefail\n\nAPI_URL=\"${PRISMFY_API_URL:-https://api.prismfy.io/v1/search}\"\nAPI_URL=\"${API_URL%/}\"\nAPI_ROOT=\"${PRISMFY_API_ROOT:-}\"\nAPI_ROOT=\"${API_ROOT%/}\"","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"9cb0c1f6893050ddcfefd4e254516908445da0f904cb1047a63da1c4c6d95fce","occurrences":[{"file":"contact-find.sh","start_line":4,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-8de3d08ce5984d37a36e33ba70bcc0c5","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"contact-find.sh","start_line":223,"end_line":null},"finding":"curl -m 20 -fsS \"$API_URL\" \\\n      -H \"Authorization: Bearer $PRISMFY_API_KEY\" \\\n      -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n      -d ","explanation":"The code performs an authenticated POST request to an external service containing assembled search queries derived from person/company/domain inputs. Because this skill is specifically designed to discover contact details, the transmitted payload may include personal names and employer associations, making third-party exfiltration of user-supplied reconnaissance data a meaningful privacy risk.","remediation":"Gate outbound requests behind explicit notice and consent, validate that users intend third-party lookup, and reduce payload contents to the minimum necessary. Consider allowing only approved API endpoints, adding configuration to disable external requests in sensitive environments, and documenting the external data flow clearly.","code_snippet":"  while (( attempt < max_attempts )); do\n    attempt=$((attempt + 1))\n    err=\"$(mktemp)\"\n    if response=\"$(curl -m 20 -fsS \"$API_URL\" \\\n      -H \"Authorization: Bearer $PRISMFY_API_KEY\" \\\n      -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n      -d \"$payload\" 2>\"$err\")\"; then","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"5b3e90970da12ae5331cd5fc45bcd4d82b3885995ec489dd8144bb9c86f56cea","occurrences":[{"file":"contact-find.sh","start_line":223,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-a0bd046d896f4c65bbadb5cab2050630","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"contact-find.sh","start_line":223,"end_line":226},"finding":null,"explanation":"The script sends user-supplied person, company, domain, and role data to a third-party Prismfy API without any user-facing disclosure or consent mechanism. In a contact-discovery skill, these queries can contain personal data or sensitive business targeting information, so undisclosed external transmission creates a real privacy and data-handling risk even if it is central to the feature.","remediation":"Add explicit disclosure that search inputs are sent to Prismfy, document what fields are transmitted, and require user/operator consent before submitting person-identifying queries. Minimize transmitted data where possible, provide a local dry-run/preview mode, and document retention and privacy expectations for the third-party service.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"contact-find.sh","start_line":223,"end_line":226}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-ffdc254996274d4aaf9b54f39eb9a929","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"contact-find.sh","start_line":82,"end_line":82},"finding":null,"explanation":"The code reads PRISMFY_API_KEY from the environment and uses it for authenticated requests, but it provides no warning in comments, help text, or runtime output that a sensitive credential is required and will be used. This falls under the code-file criterion for access 